DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The cceerrttccttll utility manages the list of TLS Certificate Authorities that
     are trusted by applications that use OpenSSL.

     Flags:

     --DD _d_e_s_t_d_i_r
           Specify the DESTDIR (overriding values from the environment).

     --dd _d_i_s_t_b_a_s_e
           Specify the DISTBASE (overriding values from the environment).

     --MM _m_e_t_a_l_o_g
           Specify the path of the METALOG file (default: $DESTDIR/METALOG).

     --nn    No-Op mode, do not actually perform any actions.

     --vv    Be verbose, print details about actions before performing them.

     --UU    Unprivileged mode, do not change the ownership of created links.
           Do record the ownership in the METALOG file.

     Primary command functions:

     lliisstt       List all currently trusted certificate authorities.

     uunnttrruusstteedd  List all currently untrusted certificates.

     rreehhaasshh     Rebuild the list of trusted certificate authorities by scan‐
                ning all directories in TRUSTPATH and all untrusted certifi‐
                cates in UNTRUSTPATH.  A symbolic link to each trusted cer‐
                tificate is placed in CERTDESTDIR and each untrusted certifi‐
                cate in UNTRUSTDESTDIR.

     uunnttrruusstt    Add the specified file to the untrusted list.

     ttrruusstt      Remove the specified file from the untrusted list.

